
# Abstract concepts

concept
    nothing
    something
    someone

    # Weather components. rain/snow/fog/wind carry a strength_measurement;
    # sky carries a sky_condition.
    weather             (obs) (tar @excl)
        rain            (tar @excl strength_measurement)
        snow            (tar @excl strength_measurement)
        fog             (tar @excl strength_measurement)
        wind            (tar @excl strength_measurement)
        sky             (tar @excl sky_condition)
        thunder         (obs) (tar @excl strength_measurement)
        temperature     (obs) (tar @excl)

    phrase
        yes
        no

    # Sidedness. Used by sided actions (REACH_FOR, GRASP, ARM_DRINK, ...) to
    # designate which arm/hand engages. The (side ?x) rule-function evaluates
    # to one of these by reading /side off the symbol's kind.
    side
        left  (side left)
        right (side right)

    availability        (sub building)  (tar @excl)
        for_sale
        for_rent
        off_the_market

    legal_right
        property        (sub being)

    condition           (tar @excl)
        alive
        dead
        # Physical incapacity distinct from sleep (alertness sleepy) and
        # from death. Bedridden / drugged / knocked-out NPCs read
        # `unconscious` until they recover or die. Distinct from the
        # `physical_mobility` derived belief which captures observable
        # locomotion level over time.
        unconscious

    alertness           (tar @excl)
        alert
        sleepy

    # Observable locomotion level - the physical-mobility state, mirrored
    # directly as a belief (like `condition` / `alertness`; no separate
    # relation). Derived in hsim_derive::classify_physical_mobility from
    # condition + leg-wound state + age. Distinct from `alertness` (sleep /
    # wake) and from `condition` (alive / dead / unconscious):
    # physical_mobility captures what an NPC can DO physically when
    # conscious. The bedridden value covers both genuine incapacity
    # (severe injury) and the social state of staying-in-bed;
    # physical_mobility being derived means the same symbol can mean both
    # as the substrate behind it varies.
    physical_mobility   (tar @excl)
        mobile
        crutch_assisted
        wheelchair_bound
        bedridden

    # Short-lived self-belief markers. The target of the
    # `transient_marker` verb-state in States.mon - a single generic
    # state replacing what would otherwise be four scattered
    # patterns (recent-incident cooldowns, stalking prep markers,
    # skill-practice tickers, substance-administering progress).
    # Minted with a per-kind decay; checked by `has_recent_marker` in
    # shared_functions/markers. The aux slot carries the focus (the
    # other party / domain / substance), so an actor may hold many
    # transient_marker beliefs concurrently - one per (kind, focus)
    # pair. Extend by adding a sub-kind here and a mint site in the
    # consuming PR (PR-A's recent_incident, PR-B's stalk_target,
    # PR-skill-life's practice, PR-C's administering).
    marker_kind
        # PR-A bonded / public incident per-pair cooldown
        # (~3 months).
        recent_incident
        # PR-B perpetration prep marker; actor has been
        # observing victim's movements (~30 days). Subsequent
        # perpetration rolls read this for the surprise modifier.
        stalk_target
        # PR-C drugging / poisoning progress marker. Aux carries
        # the substance kind; cumulative-lethal-dose terminals
        # decrement against this counter.
        administering
        # PR-skill-life: an actor exercised a domain via
        # perpetration / leisure / profession / apprenticeship /
        # club / education. Aux carries the domain. Read by
        # `skill_atrophies.hse` to suppress atrophy (~12 months).
        practice

    # Existential-frame taxonomy. The target of the `life_aim` drive in
    # States.mon: what an NPC wants their LIFE to amount to. Distinct
    # from `calling` (the specific DOMAIN one wants to excel in - music,
    # engineering, soldiering): same musician (calling=music) can hold
    # life_aim=wealth_aim (mercenary success), life_aim=legacy_aim (be
    # remembered), or life_aim=belonging_aim (just play in the local pub
    # band). Derived annually by hsim_derive::classify_life_aim from
    # substrate (Big Five + Dark Tetrad + class trajectory + bond counts
    # + worship). NOT @excl - the classifier explicitly end-dates the
    # prior dominant life_aim belief on a qualitative shift (PR-aim-
    # history), so multi-decade life_aim history is queryable as
    # repeated {@self life_aim ?} beliefs with non-overlapping intervals.
    life_aim            (tar)
        legacy_aim
        wealth_aim
        piety_aim
        respectability_aim
        autonomy_aim
        power_aim
        belonging_aim

    # Unified domain axis (PR-skill-life). ONE hierarchical taxonomy that
    # `interest`, `skilled_in`, and `calling` (States.mon) all target as three
    # progressive bands on the same axis: casual pull -> earned competence ->
    # life mission. They COMPOSE (an NPC may hold all three on one domain).
    # Replaces the former separate `interest` / `skill_kind` / `field_of_study`
    # enums; their leaves are re-parented here unchanged (the `medicine`
    # duplicate that lived in both skill_kind and field_of_study is deduped to
    # one leaf). `t_ontology::is_a` answers "any martial skill?" / "any academic
    # field?" in one query. The semantic categories group the practicable
    # competences (academic_field / performance_art / martial / illicit / sport)
    # and the non-practicable topical interests (avocation / devotional / civic)
    # an NPC may hold an `interest` in without ever being `skilled_in` it.
    domain
        # Studied disciplines (former field_of_study) + scholarly topics.
        academic_field
            classics
            engineering
            medicine
            law
            theology
            commerce
            natural_science
            accountancy
            navigation
            husbandry
            primary_school_curriculum
            secondary_school_curriculum
            history
            science
        # Expressive / cultural arts.
        performance_art
            music
            theatre
            literature
        # Combat / physical skills (former skill_kind combat leaves).
        martial
            marksmanship
            knife_fighting
            swordsmanship
            pugilism
            wrestling
            horsemanship
            riding
        # Criminal competences (former skill_kind operational leaves).
        illicit
            poisoning_knowledge
            forgery
            lockpicking
            climbing
            evading
            detecting
        # Physical recreation (the `sports` interest). NOT the standalone
        # `sport` competition-discipline enum below (cricket / rowing / ...),
        # which is the achievement target of participated_in / won.
        athletics
            sports
        # Topical interests one holds without practising a skill.
        avocation
            antiques
        devotional
            religion
            spiritualism
        civic
            suffrage

    # Competence-level enum - the /aux of `skilled_in` beliefs. Novice
    # is the entry tier; trained takes years of practice; expert is the
    # cap reachable through profession tenure or apprenticeship-to-
    # master. Future tier (master) may land if a 4th band is needed for
    # exceptional NPCs.
    competence_level    (tar @excl)
        novice
        trained
        expert

    # (Relational stance no longer uses band-kind aux taxonomies; the continuous
    # warmth/esteem/trust/attraction scalar projects directly to infinitive
    # verb-state beliefs - like/dislike/admire/... - declared in States.mon's
    # (stance) block. See Docs/social/relational_stance_plan.md sections 3, 5.4.)

    death_cause         (tar @excl)
        disease
        accident
        old_age
        childbirth
        violence

    # Specific diseases an NPC can have. Distinct
    # from `death_cause disease` which is the cause-of-death enum value;
    # this taxonomy names the specific pathology (consumption /
    # cholera / etc.). Future env attr `disease` (kind, /reason or
    # /imperceptible per knowledge_design_notes.md - reading it requires
    # a DIAGNOSE action by a competent physician, not passive
    # perception) will hold one of these values per sick NPC. Sub-kinds
    # are starter content for 1897 medical reality; extend as content
    # demands.
    disease
        consumption
        cholera
        smallpox
        typhus
        dysentery
        influenza
        scarlet_fever
        pneumonia

    # Observable symptoms. Distinct from disease:
    # symptoms are what others SEE (cough / fever / pallor / weakness);
    # the disease is the diagnosis a physician INFERS from symptoms. Each
    # leaf has a corresponding env attr on body archetypes (mech obs);
    # the disease attr is /reason or /imperceptible. Starter set; extend
    # as content demands.
    symptom
        cough
        fever
        pallor
        weakness
        rash
        chills

    # Cause-of-death narrative witnesses form when
    # perceiving a death scene (vs death_cause, the objective cause). Used
    # in `circumstances_of_death` beliefs that F2 gossip carries
    # village-wide; the "staged story" emerges from observers agreeing on
    # a particular incident kind. Extensible as new staging shapes are
    # authored.
    incident
        burglary
        domestic_violence
        accident
        duel
        illness_complication

    # Region mood components (the mood_kinds attr is plural - a region carries
    # several at once, so no @excl).
    mood
        anti_aristocratic
        anti_outsider
        plague_fear
        pro_reform
        war_weariness

    # Personal emotion - transient affective states, held as the noun-state
    # {subject emotion <kind>}. /sub human, so {?other emotion anger} is a
    # valid held belief (theory of mind for free). Non-@excl: emotions
    # coexist (joy about one thing, grief about another). /tar is omitted, so
    # the target defaults to emotion's own subkinds. The directed "about"
    # focus rides in the belief's aux field. See Docs/emotion_sim_plan.md.
    emotion             (sub human)
        joy
        pride
        hope
        relief
        gratitude
        affection
        grief
        distress
        anger
        fear
        shame
        guilt
        envy
        jealousy
        disgust
        contempt
        # admiration: positive esteem - looking UP at competence / honour /
        # virtue (the sibling of contempt). Minted by honour_act; the Class I
        # stance coupling routes it to esteem+ (relational_stance_plan 4.1).
        admiration
        # longing: the felt pull of attraction - the transient affective surface
        # of the durable attraction scalar (fancy/desire/crave verb-states).
        # Minted by the standing attraction driver toward a mate-valued target
        # (relational_stance_plan 4.3 / 12.6). Named `longing`, not `desire`, to
        # avoid colliding with the `desire` attraction verb-state label. No stance
        # coupling row: the attraction scalar is already driven by mate-value, so
        # this is a pure feeling (mood / NLG surface), not a stance re-driver.
        longing

    # Personal pressure - second-order standing motivational loads that build
    # when beliefs + drives + appraisals + constraints converge (plan section
    # 10.3-AFFECT item A). Parallel to emotion in shape - {subject pressure
    # <kind>} with the directed focus in aux - but with multi-week to
    # multi-year salience windows (vs emotion's hours to days) and a
    # different mood contribution (pressures feed the `stress` dimension, not
    # contentment / agitation). Non-@excl: pressures stack - the layered
    # motive a deliberation event reads IS the stacked pressure set.
    pressure            (sub human)
        status_loss
        attachment_loss
        autonomy_loss
        exposure_risk
        resource_scarcity
        humiliation
        injustice
        moral_violation
        existential_threat
        obligation_strain
        rivalry_pressure

    # Justifying narratives - the cognitive frames an NPC holds to make a
    # past or planned harmful act acceptable to themselves (plan section
    # 10.3-AFFECT item E). Target of the `justify` attitude
    # (States.mon): {@self justify they_deserved_it /aux <victim>}. The held
    # narrative discounts inhibition; a guilty NPC's justify beliefs are
    # queryable through interrogation in isim. Different perpetrators hold
    # different narratives; a non-guilty NPC holds none.
    narrative
        they_deserved_it
        i_had_no_choice
        it_was_necessary
        everyone_does_this
        i_was_protecting_kin
        they_are_subhuman
        the_law_is_unjust
        self_defense

    # Role-identities an NPC self-identifies as. Held as {@self identity
    # <role>} self-beliefs; derived by hsim_derive::classify_identities from
    # substrate state (kids -> parent, spouse -> spouse, job -> worker,
    # church member -> christian, class + gender -> gentleman / lady, job
    # kind -> merchant / servant / soldier / steward, Dark Tetrad attr ->
    # machiavellian / sadist, low assertiveness composite -> coward);
    # future PRs add explicit identity-adoption events. Read by the
    # deliberate synthesizer to anchor floor branches (more identities ->
    # more anchored -> more likely to forgive / do_nothing); by
    # categorize() to shift thresholds when an anchor's parties overlap
    # the appraiser's identity-relevant relations (a parent identity makes
    # child-related construals more salient); by the justify pick to bias
    # which narrative an actor reaches for (a parent reaches for
    # i_was_protecting_kin, a christian-priest for it_was_necessary); and
    # by perpetration.hsc method rows' :id-dampens / :id-boosts to bias
    # method selection (a gentleman dampens public_confront, a sadist
    # boosts cook_alive).
    # Non-@excl - an NPC's composite identity IS the held set.
    # Atom names are `<X>_role` to avoid colliding with existing kinds of
    # the same bare name (parent / spouse are relationship bonds;
    # merchant / steward are job kinds; etc.). The `_role` suffix reads
    # naturally when minted: `{@self identity parent_role}` = "I identify
    # as a parent."
    role
        parent_role
        spouse_role
        worker_role
        christian_role
        gentleman_role
        lady_role
        merchant_role
        servant_role
        soldier_role
        steward_role
        # Dark Tetrad and trait-composite identities.
        # machiavellian / sadist read the homonymous Dark Tetrad attr
        # against a tunable threshold in situations.hsc; coward fires on
        # EITHER (low assertiveness AND high withdrawal) OR (high
        # inhibition AND not-respectable).
        machiavellian_role
        sadist_role
        coward_role
        # Skill-driven trade / talent identities (PR-skill-life S8). Derived by
        # classify_identities from a held {@self skilled_in <domain>} at >=
        # trained: physician <- medicine, lawyer <- law, scholar <- any other
        # academic_field, soldier (soldier_role above) <- martial, musician <-
        # music, artist <- other performance_art (theatre / literature),
        # sportsman <- athletics. The competence (not the job title) confers the
        # identity, so a trained-in-medicine apothecary still identifies as a
        # physician. Composite (non-@excl): a polymath holds several.
        physician_role
        lawyer_role
        scholar_role
        musician_role
        artist_role
        sportsman_role

    # Interests are now `{@self interest <domain>}` beliefs (the casual-pull
    # band of the unified `domain` axis above); `interest` is an explicit
    # verb-state in States.mon. The former standalone `interest` topic enum was
    # folded into `domain` (PR-skill-life): music/theatre/literature ->
    # performance_art, history/science -> academic_field, riding -> martial,
    # sports -> athletics, religion/spiritualism -> devotional, antiques ->
    # avocation, suffrage -> civic. Still seeded as hereditary self-beliefs in
    # mx_make_human and grown / shed by interest_acquired / interest_lost.

    # Competitive sports - the target of the participated_in / won achievement
    # beliefs (States.mon), written by the sporting_event hsim event. A `sport`
    # is the competition discipline; distinct from the `sports` interest above.
    sport
        cricket
        rowing
        rugby
        horse_racing

    # Games - the thing one plays (a hand of cards, a frame of billiards). A
    # game is a group activity OBJECT: each occasion is a per-mind game object
    # of one of these kinds (a Mental Object per knowledge_design_notes), wired
    # {@self play_game <game>} + {<game> participant <co-player>}. The
    # `(gambling)` FACET (not a kind branch) marks the money games, cross-
    # cutting the taxonomy - a card_game may or may not be played for stakes.
    # The standing DISPOSITION to gamble is the `gambling_addiction` attr
    # (common.arc), not a kind here.
    game
        card_game
            poker     (facets gambling)
            blackjack (facets gambling)
            whist
            bridge
        billiards
        dominoes      (facets gambling)

    # Intoxicants - the abstract substance an NPC can form a `craving` for
    # (the (drive) block in States.mon) and that the drinking behaviour events
    # act on. `alcohol` is the abstract substance; the physical `beer` prop
    # (Objects.mon) is a separate, concrete layer.
    substance
        alcohol
        # Cardiac glycoside; the canonical poison in
        # the case study. Concrete bottles are `prop` entities containing it.
        digitalis

    living_arrangement  (sub human)  (tar ? @excl)
        owner           (tar human|org @excl)
        houseguest
        renting

    status              (tar ? @excl)
        examined
        accepted
        rejected

    capacity            (tar ? @excl)
        pub_patron

    activity
        bartending
        
    org_pos
        apprenticeship
        membership          (sub human)
        job                 (sub human)
            editor
            printer
            journalist
            banker
            landlord
            industrialist
            principal
            merchant
            apothecary
            proprietor
            solicitor
            physician
            priest
            clerk
            teacher
            engineer
            surgeon
            typist
            barber
            gardener
            cook
            farmer
            nurse
            # Estate manager job-kind. Standard
            # per-mind job-object pattern: {?npc job ?j_obj} +
            # {?j_obj isa [k steward]}. Holds the day-to-day authority over
            # an `estate` org (Concepts.mon, business sub-kind).
            steward
            shop_clerk
            waiter
            maid
            bartender
            factory_worker
            house_agent
            # Heads of the public cultural institutions (gov sub-kinds above):
            # the librarian runs the library, the curator the museum. The
            # meeting_hall + sports_ground are run by a clerk (no bespoke job).
            librarian
            curator
            # University don (PR-education). Head + teaching staff of the
            # `university` org (org > edu > university). class_floor upper -
            # the professions' apex. Confers no single domain skill (a don's
            # competence came from their own degree, minted at graduation),
            # so occupations.hsc gives it no (domain ...).
            professor
            # Phase 9 senior_appointment hires public-org appointees under
            # this kind. Distinct from clerk so prestige / pretty-print can
            # render a senior official differently from an ordinary employee.
            # ("Holding a post" is just this job-state - there is no separate
            # office-as-position concept.)
            official
            # Performer parent-kind (Phase 9 dialogue) - witnesses whose job
            # is_a performer hold an audience-aware self-conception that
            # gates the theatrical register decoration.
            performer
                actor
                singer
                musician
                magician
                preacher
                lecturer


    # level grades a human, or a job / org_pos. A trainee clerk is
    # {@self job ?j} + {?j level trainee}.
    level               (sub human|org_pos)  (tar @excl)
            trainee
            apprentice
            junior
            regular
            senior
            org_head
    unit
        social
            family          (sub human)  (tar @excl)
    movement
        political
            suffrage
    org
        edu
            apprenticeship
            private_school
            state_school
            university
        gov
            church
            hospital
            agency
                land_registry
                company_registry
            # Public civic / cultural institutions. Founded + minimally staffed
            # at sim start by the govt-bootstrap pass (public_orgs.hsc), each
            # occupying its own building kind (businesses.hsc). They are the
            # venues the interest activity lane sends enthusiasts to (L5):
            # library <- literature/history/science, museum <- antiques,
            # meeting_hall <- suffrage + the civic default, sports_ground <-
            # sports/riding.
            library
            museum
            meeting_hall
            sports_ground
        com
            club
                # Athletic clubs - founded procedurally (k_foundable_club_kinds).
                athletic_club
                    race_club
                    rugby_union
                # Social/gentlemen's clubs - the named institutions (the Albion,
                # St-Revi, Mariner's, Meridian House, the Foundry) are specific
                # pre-placed instances, not procedurally founded.
                social_club
            business
                factory
                bank
                shipping_agent
                insurance_co
                solicitor_firm
                house_agency
                newspaper
                pawnbroker
                hotel
                restaurant
                bookseller
                grocer
                pub
                apothecary
                barbershop
                antiques_shop
                theatre
                # A property business. Covers both the landed / agricultural
                # estate and the residential-letting company a landlord runs
                # (hsim::become_landlord founds one and hires the founder as its
                # `landlord`). Owns property, generates revenue, employs people,
                # and is sold / inherited / dissolved by the ordinary org
                # lifecycle - being a landlord is therefore not a special case.
                estate

    # Fields of study were folded into the unified `domain` axis (PR-skill-life):
    # the former field_of_study leaves now live under `domain > academic_field`.
    # The `study` / `diploma` relations and `skilled_in` (States.mon) target
    # `domain` (a field-of-study is an academic_field sub-kind of domain).

    # ----------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Derived situations (F3.3) - a category ("what sort of X"), each an @excl
    # noun-state classified from several dimensions by an F3.5 classifier.
    # Never authored; computed and cached. F3.6 removed the coarse social_class
    # attr: class_situation is now the sole class concept, a belief seeded by
    # mx_make_human (upper/middle/lower). Turning it into a fully derived
    # belief - the eight-value form, classified from prestige + breeding +
    # wealth - is future work and needs founder-seeded title/lineage/education
    # grounding. (`stable` / `struggling` recur across situations - a
    # deliberate scoped homonym, resolved by the field's /tar, like `medium`.)
    # ----------------------------------------------------------------------
    economic_situation       (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        destitute
        poor
        struggling
        stable
        comfortable
        prosperous
        wealthy
    respectability_situation (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        exemplary
        respectable
        questionable
        disreputable
        scandalous
    class_situation          (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        upper
        middle
        lower
    health_situation         (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        robust
        frail
        ailing
        invalid
    social_trajectory        (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        rising
        stable
        declining
    life_satisfaction        (sub human)  (tar @excl)
        fulfilled
        content
        secure_but_hollow
        struggling
        loner
        adrift

    # Derived archetypes (F3.4) - a named conjunction over situations and
    # dimensions; non-@excl, an NPC may match several. Prototype kinds are
    # added with their classifiers - these four are F3.7 / Phase 7 consumers.
    prototype                (sub human)
        deserving_poor
        undeserving_poor
        self_made_man
        nouveau_riche
        drunkard

    message
        declaration
        property_description
        article
        advert
        chapter
    payment
        wage
        annual_wage

    # Reified act-categories - the context-free "what kind of act" tags
    # that the appraisal pipeline reads off any anchor belief (Docs/
    # emotion_sim_plan.md section 2.4 + plan section 10.3-AFFECT item J).
    # FLAT vocabulary: no hierarchy among the categories - every leaf state
    # / action enumerates which categories it falls under via a
    # (construed_act tag1 tag2 ...) sexpr at declaration time. is_a checks
    # against the construed_act ROOT recognize any of these as appraisal
    # categories; specific dispatch is by direct kind comparison. The set
    # mixes (a) "what was done" categories (wrong, help, honour, intimacy,
    # ...), (b) outcome categories (suffer_loss, achieve), and (c) the
    # cross-cutting umbrellas (wrong over harm/slight/appropriation/...,
    # help over aid/provision, ...) - all flat siblings rather than nested.
    # Wronging branch  : wrong_act (umbrella) over harm/slight/appropriation/
    #                    coercion/abandonment/betray/expose/threaten - all of
    #                    them are flavors of "bad things to someone".
    # Helping branch   : help_act (umbrella) over aid (direct assistance) and
    #                    provision (giving alms / gifts / drink).
    # Honour branch    : honour_act (public recognition) plus commitment_act
    #                    (keeping a promise IS honouring).
    # Intimacy         : intimacy_act on its own. Betray-by-diversion mints a
    #                    separate betray_act construal in observer minds via
    #                    categorize()'s structural test.
    # Outcomes         : suffer_loss_act (patient lost something) and
    #                    achieve_act (actor succeeded) - outcome-based,
    #                    minted directly by hsim events when relevant.
    # neutral_act      : legacy "do not appraise" tag - kept so .act files
    #                    declaring `nature = neutral_act` keep parsing.
    #                    New code: just omit (construed_act ...) entirely.
    construed_act       (+ sub human)
        wrong_act
        harm_act
        slight_act
        appropriation_act
        coercion_act
        abandonment_act
        betray_act
        expose_act
        threaten_act
        help_act
        aid_act
        provision_act
        honour_act
        commitment_act
        intimacy_act
        suffer_loss_act
        achieve_act
        neutral_act
        # rivalrous_act: actor competes with patient for a shared scarce
        # resource (post, partner, inheritance). Distinct from slight_act
        # (which is unprovoked affront) - rivalry is positional. Mints
        # rivalry_pressure on the outcompeted patient via the reaction
        # row in appraisal.hsc. Placed at end to keep older taxonomy
        # kind ids stable.
        rivalrous_act

    sky_condition
        clear
        overcast
        cloudy

    strength_measurement
        none
        light
        medium
        heavy

    mass_measurement
        weight
    
    # Sexual orientation - a kind-typed /feel attr (common.arc). Genetic;
    # learned of others only by a spouse / immediate family (believe_about
    # Band 4). The Big Five personality aspects and the dark tetrad are 0..1
    # float attrs, not kinds, so they need no taxonomy here.
    sexual_orient           (tar @excl)
        hetero
        bi
        homo

    cultural_aspect
        title
        nationality         (sub human)  (tar @excl)
            english
            irish
            st_revieran
            french

    physical_quality
        color               (tar @excl)
            blue
            brown
            green
            grey
            hazel
            black
            red
            auburn
            blonde
            white
        gender              (tar @excl)
            male
            female
        appearance          (tar @excl)
            ugly
            plain_looking
            beautiful
        girth               (tar @excl)
            thin
            medium
            fat
        height              (tar @excl)
            short
            medium
            tall

    blood_type          (obs) (tar @excl)
        A
        B
        AB
        O

    # game_role distinguishes the player-vs-NPC dispatch the engine
    # reads from the social-identity beliefs (the `role` identity
    # taxonomy above: parent / spouse / worker / christian / ...) that
    # the appraisal pipeline reads.
    game_role           (tar @excl)
        player
        nonplayer

    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Relational states. A noun is automatically a state, so each is
    # declared once here; States.mon holds only non-noun verb states.
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------

    # Transaction states.
    price               (tar @excl)
    item                (obs) (tar object)
    view                (obs) (sub human)  (tar @excl object)

    # Kinship and social bonds - subject and target are both human. //noun
    # makes every role explicitly a noun, so the bond decorations below
    # (relation flags) do not trip define()'s noun-vs-relation inference.
    relationship        (+ sub human)  (+ tar human)  (+ noun)
        parent          (inclusive_bond)
        mother          (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)
        father          (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)
        brother         (inclusive_bond)
        sister          (inclusive_bond)
        sibling         (inclusive_bond)
        half_sibling    (inclusive_bond)
        grandmother     (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)
        grandfather     (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)
        grandparent     (inclusive_bond)
        grandchild      (inclusive_bond)
        aunt            (inclusive_bond)
        uncle           (inclusive_bond)
        niece           (inclusive_bond)
        nephew          (inclusive_bond)
        cousin          (inclusive_bond)
        mother_in_law   (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)
        father_in_law   (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)
        parent_in_law   (inclusive_bond)
        sister_in_law   (inclusive_bond)
        brother_in_law  (inclusive_bond)
        sibling_in_law  (inclusive_bond)
        daughter_in_law (inclusive_bond)
        son_in_law      (inclusive_bond)
        child_in_law    (inclusive_bond)
        stepmother      (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)
        stepfather      (tar @excl)  (inclusive_bond)
        stepchild       (inclusive_bond)
        child           (inclusive_bond)
        # Guardianship. {?guardian ward ?ward_npc} reads
        # "guardian is the legal guardian of ward". Inclusive bond
        # (multiple wards possible). The case study's Ashcombe/Clara pair
        # uses this for the pre-perpetration relationship.
        ward            (inclusive_bond)
        spouse          (tar @excl)  (exclusive_bond)
        fiancee         (tar @excl)  (exclusive_bond)
        lover           (inclusive_bond)
        friend          (inclusive_bond)
        acquaintance
        neighbour
        close_to
        relied_on_by
        respected_by
        enemy
        love                    (tar ?)  (exclusive_bond)
        # Directed competitive bond. May be
        # asymmetric (A fixates on B; B indifferent). Sourced by
        # rivalry-pressure-driving events (lost-job-to, outbid-by,
        # out-courted-by). Read by deliberation affinity rows and by
        # appraisal to weight slight_act reactions higher when the
        # source is a held rival.
        rival                   (inclusive_bond)
        # Conspiracy bond. Subject = principal
        # (recruiter), target = helper. Aux carries the embedded
        # goal-fact that `recruit` minted into the helper's mind.
        # Closes the loop on the existing `recruit (tar human) (aux ?)`
        # behaviour label - recruit is the ACT, accomplice is the
        # ongoing BOND.
        accomplice              (aux ?)
        # Co-equity bond in a venture. Symmetric -
        # minted on both sides when the partnership is formed. Aux
        # carries the org. Distinct from `founder` (one-shot
        # constitutive, @excl) and `employer` (subordinate relation).
        # Same org may have many partners.
        business_partner        (aux org)

    marriage_desirability   (tar ? @excl)

    birthplace          (sub human)  (tar structure @excl)

    # Vocational / educational / societal states (subject is a human).
    vocational_state    (+ sub human)
        retire              (tar ? @excl)
        home                (tar structure @excl)
        # Work life-cycle. job and level are noun-states (declared in the
        # org_pos / level taxonomy higher up); only the non-noun relations
        # are declared here. employer is the worker's org; master is the
        # master a youth trains under.
        employer            (noun) (tar org @excl)   (inclusive_bond)
        master              (noun) (tar human @excl)   (inclusive_bond)
        # Education life-cycle. study names the field a pupil reads and the
        # school they read it at; schooling is the schooling-level outcome
        # left behind when the pupil leaves. A graduate's credential is the
        # `diploma` document noun (Objects.mon) - already a state, so no
        # diploma relation is declared here.
        study               (tar @excl academic_field)    (aux org)
        schooling           (tar ? @excl)

    # Property holdings: a holder's owned buildings and land are recorded as
    # repeated singular {holder building <building>} / {holder land <land>}
    # beliefs. `building` (Objects.mon) and `land` (Spaces.mon) are nouns and
    # so are already states, so no relation is declared here.

    # States describing an organisation (subject is the org mental object).
    # employee is repeated once per worker; record points at the org's
    # articles_of_incorporation document.
    org_state           (+ sub org)
        informal_name       (tar ? @excl)
        founder             (tar human @excl)
        head_pos            (tar org_pos @excl)
        workplace           (tar space|structure @excl)
        employee            (tar human)
        vacancy             (tar job)
        record              (tar document @excl)

    # Document -> org back-link: the inverse of org_state's `record`. Lets any
    # mind reconstruct its own per-mind org object from the stable
    # articles_of_incorporation env anchor, via
    # mx_imagine_or_recall(orgkind, mx_observe(articles), "declares_org").
    declares_org        (sub document)  (tar org @excl)

    # Building -> tenant link: the queryable form of a lease, whose contract
    # records are the private lease_agreement documents kept at both parties'
    # premises. @excl - one ongoing tenant at a time (a re-lease opens a fresh
    # interval after the prior one ends).
    tenant              (sub building|space)  (tar human|org @excl)

    # Building -> occupant link: everyone habitually present in the building,
    # regardless of legal title - household members and staff at a home,
    # employees at a workplace. Distinct from owner / tenant (which are about
    # title); non-@excl, since a building has many occupants and a person
    # occupies both their home and their workplace.
    occupant            (sub building|space)  (tar human)

    # States describing an activity-object.
    activity_state
        participant         (tar human)
        todo                (tar task)
